    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a8e6fe94_0f3914fe",
        "filename": "chip/g/board_space.h",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 27,
      "author": {
        "id": 1256783
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-08-02T09:11:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That is a great question. As far as I can tell, the discussions have stalled as there is no single owner for the RMA process. My guess would be that this will not be resolved until the RMA process for the first ZTE-enabled device is defined.\n\nI was thinking that if we are at least sure of the size, then this change can land, and we can update the use of this space later, when we are more clear on which bits mean what.\n\nIf that is not an appropriate approach, then I think it\u0027s probably best to leave this change until the RMA process is defined.",
      "parentUuid": "87e68864_4f078078",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 27,
        "startChar": 1,
